      "writtenOn": "2024-12-10T22:14:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t the minimal frame size actually a bit shorter compared to kLeCocMtuMin ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "954aa0239ea3ddd636d1f93c4b2cedc3faa7e129",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e6b007a_fc86b9b1",
        "filename": "system/gd/hal/socket_hal_android.cc",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1959878
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-11T01:24:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we are constrained by the RFCOMM spec here so can\u0027t go below 23 bytes according to this [table 5.1](https://www.bluetooth.com/wp-content/uploads/Files/Specification/HTML/RFCOMM_v1.1/RFCOMM_v1.1/out/en/index-en.html#UUID-2ba3724c-f013-72b8-1b6c-bc7a8686416b_N1717529873665). \n\nMy understanding is that `kRfcommFrameSizeMin` is just used to make sure the socket capabilities for RFCOMM are within the specs, but it is unlikely that the negotiated max frame size will not comply with the L2CAP mtu. I will double check it when I work on the CL for determining the RFCOMM max frame size in btif.",
      "parentUuid": "9438b11a_ba6784d7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "954aa0239ea3ddd636d1f93c4b2cedc3faa7e129",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a96f6cc_9a960ccb",
        "filename": "system/gd/hal/socket_hal_android.cc",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-11T19:42:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that either one of the values may be false, but they probably shouldn\u0027t be equal ... I haven\u0027t checked the spec values though.",
      "parentUuid": "3e6b007a_fc86b9b1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "954aa0239ea3ddd636d1f93c4b2cedc3faa7e129",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9394e6e1_6fc25bef",
        "filename": "system/gd/hal/socket_hal_android.cc",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1959878
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-14T00:20:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@jaydenk@google.com IIUC for the RFCOMM socket it is not using `kLeCocMtuMin` to determin the lower limit of the L2CAP MTU, and looks like for the current L2CAP MTU lower limit it is using [L2CAP_MIN_MTU](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/stack/l2cap/l2c_api.cc;drc\u003d9bb9a8a16bd3db579880e1340786eb5104deb9d8;l\u003d165) which is 48. If this is the case then the value 23 here for RFCOMM seems to be safe.",
      "parentUuid": "4a96f6cc_9a960ccb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "954aa0239ea3ddd636d1f93c4b2cedc3faa7e129",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0350686a_b271d609",
        "filename": "system/gd/hal/socket_hal_android.cc",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1959861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-14T01:24:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right. The minimum L2CAP MTU are different between Classic and LE. Current defitions, `kLeCocMtuMin`, `kLeCocMtuMax`, `kRfcommFrameSizeMin`, and `kRfcommFrameSizeMax` are correct as per Core and RFCOMM specification.\n\nOverall Minimun L2CAP MTU in Core Spec.\n```\nAll L2CAP implementations shall support a minimum MTU of 48 octets over the ACL-U logical link and 23 octets\nover the LE-U logical link\n```\n\nRFCOMM Maximum Frame Size in RFCOMM Spec.\n```\nMaximum Frame Size (N1) Default: 127 (negotiable range 23 – 32767)\n```\n\nLE COC MTU in Core Spec.\n```\nThe MTU field specifies the maximum SDU size (in octets) that the L2CAP layer\nentity sending the L2CAP_LE_CREDIT_BASED_CONNECTION_REQ packet can\nreceive on this channel. L2CAP implementations shall support a minimum MTU size\nof 23 octets.\n```",
      "parentUuid": "9394e6e1_6fc25bef",
